Context: From Edward Thomas, "I Never Saw That Land Before" and from Tu Fu, "Conscripts Leaving for the Frontier." Trans. Charles Budd
Answer: Chariots rumbling; horses neighing;
Soldiers shouting martial cries;
Drums are sounding; trumpets braying;
Seas of glittering spears arise.
Generate a question based on the above information and the corresponding answer.

Answer: I see the tracks of the railroads of the earth;
I see them welding State to State, city to city, through North America;
I see them in Great Britain, I see them in Europe;
I see them in Asia and in Africa.
Generate a question based on the above information and the corresponding answer.
